<title>HONG KONG: Amnuay says baht not under extreme pressure.</title>
<headline>Amnuay says baht not under extreme pressure.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's deputy prime minister and minister of foreign affairs Amnuay Viravan said on Monday in Hong Kong he did not believe the exchange rate was under any extreme pressure.  </p>
<p>&quot;I do not believe the exchange rate is under any extreme pressure,&quot; he told a news conference after addressing a World Economic Forum meeting in the British colony. &quot;I don't think we need to change the basket of currencies at present.&quot;</p>
<p>Amnuay said he did not want to create uncertainty in the markets.</p>
<p>The government must endeavour to create a stable environment for business interests, he said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
